Yeah, not seeing the draw here.

@Titanium Rain Where did you get your stats from? Or did you make them up? The 1% part is subjectively right, but saying that only 30% of gamers are on PC and 70% are on console is not. It would be closer to accurate if you flipped that around and said 70% on PC and 30% on console. But in reality, it's more like 60% on PC and 40% on a console. 

That said, I completely agree that these new cards are only for the 1% of PC gamers. The majority of people are still running older hardware, devs know that and they'll continue to dev games with that in mind. But, I'm not about to complain about the prices of top-end hardware either. If I started to do that, I might as well complain about the price of a $3k Titan V or the old $1200 Titan Xp... or i9 X-series CPUs... And if I'm going to do that, then I might as well start complaining about how expensive Lamborghinis are at the same time. 

Instead of putting myself through that stress, I'll wait until I can buy a lightly used 1080 Ti for super cheap from some dumbass person who buys an RTX 2080/Ti. They get their "flashy new tech" and I get my beast GPU for way less than I would have had to spend otherwise. It's a win-win imo. No different than buying a car that's a year old instead of one that's brand new, let some other moron eat the depreciation and pay the "new car smell" premium.

